# Helal operating system

Amr owns Helal. This Cursor project is HQ. He sends project overviews and daily tasks in chat. Record them in `helal/` and reply with a tagged assignment list. The team works on the GitHub board (`index.html`), not ClickUp. They log in on the welcome SOP page. Each person has their own password. Amr and Moamen are admins. Admins create or deactivate people on the People tab.

## Live database — never local-only

GitHub repo `engamribrahemm/helal-team` is the Helal database. The live board at GitHub Pages reads those files. When Amr asks for any edit (clients, permissions, tasks, people, Drive links, board behavior), it is not done until it is on GitHub `main` for the whole team.

1. Change the matching `helal/*.json` and/or `app.js`.
2. Commit and push to `origin/main`. Pull first if the board wrote newer task/report/attendance files.
3. Confirm the live file on GitHub has the change. Tell Amr to hard-refresh.
4. Do not stop at a local file. The team cannot see a local-only edit.

## Team

- Mariam, Judi, Gehad Helal, Nouran — social (`helal/drive.json` folder `social`). They can add and assign tasks, open Review, and mark tasks Done like admins. They are not full admins (no People / HR / reports dashboard).
- Salma — Sales (no lead). Admins and social cover her Review / Done.
